  "body": "### Summary\n\nCamCraft's UI gets its workbench rework, built on upstream v0.19.0. It gives the shell a light workbench theme (`horizon-day`), puts a tab row above the ribbon cells to switch machine modes in one click, gives the operation page's section tabs their own glyphs, tightens the browser's chrome and row order, and adds camera tools to the viewport's floating control ribbon.\n\nFive commits, one topic each:\n\n- `feat(ui): a light workbench theme and workspace tabs`\n- `feat(ui): the operation page's section tabs wear their own glyphs`\n- `feat(ui): a compact browser header and ordered rows`\n- `feat(ui): camera tools in the viewport's control ribbon`\n- `refactor(ui): drop the Machine ribbon cell - the workspace tabs own the switch`\n\n### What to look at\n\n- The ribbon gains a workspace tab row above the cells: one tab per machine mode in `machine_modes::MACHINE_MODES`, switching through the same undoable `LoadBuiltinMachine` the Machine door queued. The stocked door and the tabs were two doors onto one switch; the tabs won, and the SETUP group sheds the redundant \"Machine\" cell at the end. The Machine door's code path remains present but unreachable from the UI, held for a follow-up removal pass.\n- `assets/themes/horizon-day.json` is a light \"Horizon Day\" palette (base light) that users can pick from the Theme door; nothing switches the default theme - dark stays the default.\n- The section tabs in the operation pages wear purpose-drawn `sec-*` glyphs (six SVG masters, rendered at the ribbon's token size; our own artwork); the ribbon cell ink gains a tinted-palette hook with a steel-blue tint for command glyphs.\n- The viewport's floating control ribbon gains four buttons: a Perspective/Orthographic toggle (the View door's radios' true twin), and a latched Orbit/Pan/Zoom nav tool that owns the drag whatever the mouse button - a latched tool's click is no click at all.\n- The browser heads with one chrome row (a View door, Expand all / Collapse all) and the setup's furniture leads the rows: Setups, WCS, Stock, Operations, Tool list, Fixtures, Machine, Post.\n\n### Verification\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` - 772 passed. `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` - green (ui suites). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --lib --tests` - no warnings.\n\nKnown flake: the palette/assertion law tests are parallel-order dependent - a full parallel run can see a handful of them fail while `--test-threads=1` is all green; the failure set moves between runs, and serial runs pass. Nothing in this PR changes their behaviour; re-run to confirm.\n",
